>In article <1991Aug4.015226.2969@nicedel.north.de>, nyse@nicedel.north.de (Hermann Behrens) writes:
>|> PS: What Do you think is the best pet? A dragon or what?

I am partial to dragons because they are easiest to maintain.  I have had pet
minotaurs and pet cockatrices, plus some other lesser monsters, but I could
never figure out what minotaurs and cockatrices will eat.  While killing a
cockatrice is generally no big deal, the reason I tamed the minotaur in the
first place was because I was about to die while trying to fight him.  The
last thing I wanted was to have him get confused (which he did) by hunger.
So I scooted down a level.  The dragon on the other hand, the main thing
is to try to keep him from killing and eating things you wish to kill and
eat (or talk to, like a priestess!).  Also, it is highly recommended that
you zap your pet with speed monster and make invisible (only if you see
invisible), but remember if the worst happens you may have to deal with
him in this condition.  I personally love having a fast invisible pet
black dragon.  Keeps the riffraff off your back while you deal with
real problems.

